        <h1>LeetCode 3736: Minimum Moves to Equal Array Elements III (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given an integer array nums. In one move, you may increase the value of any single
                element nums[i] by 1. Return the minimum total number of moves required so that all
                elements in nums become equal.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: nums = [2,1,3]<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: Raise nums[0] from 2 to 3 (1 move). Raise nums[1] from 1 to 2 (1 move), then
                from 2 to 3 (1 move). All elements now equal 3, for a total of 3 moves.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int minMoves(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums) {
        int largest = INT_MIN;
        int total = 0;

        for (int val : nums) {
            total += val;
            largest = max(val, largest);
        }

        return nums.size() * largest - total;
    }
};</code></pre>
